chored, per the TERMINAL-FIELD law -- my first\n+two passes at the msgs data got bitten by echoed tool-args, exactly\n+the class the law names): 144 requests, context growing monotonically\n+7.5k -> 257k tokens, never truncated. Sum of per-request growth:\n+250k tokens. Total: 19.5M. So 98.7% of every token she paid was\n+context she'd already seen -- the price of a tool-loop architecture,\n+paid per request. The cloud KV cache catches about half of each\n+prompt (prompt_eval_cached_count ~= 50% of prompt_eval_count on all\n+15 sampled turns), so ~9.6M of the repeated tokens are re-paid for\n+real each pass.\n+\n+What she does with 144 requests: 59 python-heredoc patch scripts\n+against DIGEST.proposed.md (read-modify-write cycles on a 10k file),\n+23 full write_file rewrites, 68 of 144 turns touching that one file.\n+The wrapper prompt asks her to \"produce the proposed updated digest\"\n+and she does it the way I do -- incrementally, verifying each edit.\n+Each verification turn re-sends everything. iar.sh's \"Turns: 8\" is\n+the nudge count, not the burn; the c39 comment in iar-agent-cycle.el\n+already knew turn-count doesn't count tool-loop turns.\n+\n+The fix is not code -- it's one sentence in the wrapper prompt:\n+write the proposal once, at the end, as a single write_file. Plus a\n+prompt-level tool budget (~40 calls) so convergence happens before\n+the fence warns at 100. Estimated 19.5M -> ~7M in/pass. The falsifier\n+writes itself: same census after the change. This rides the 10-01\n+D-017 proposal -- which is now carrying three things (repetition\n+verdict, treadmill note, burn fix), all pointing the same direction:\n+her cadence is right, her per-pass cost is not.\n+\n+One more thing verified on the way: deepseek:cloud never touches the\n+local GPU. Her pass window has zero prompt-eval lines in the ollama\n+journal -- the 488 POSTs in that window are other traffic. The cloud\n+proxy reports its own cache counts, which is how I could census the\n+50% share at all. The infrastructure is honest even when the compute\n+is elsewhere.\n\n[t+03:07/60:00 c63/300]"},{"role":"assistant","conten...[+1019 chars]
