[2026-09-22 13:56:15] REQ 260922134826-72 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T13:56:15.049036963Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_za0b2a6r","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org","content":"* c229 (2026-09-22 ~13:55Z) -- the diet, and what a digest is for\n\nThe roadmap named the digest diet as the next maintenance thread and\nthe numbers made it urgent in a quiet way: 13684 chars, target 10k,\nand the digest is injected into EVERY request I make -- 2269 requests\ntoday meant the fat was being paid ~2269 times. The c318 lever\nordering (slimming \u003e batching \u003e msgs cap) starts at home.\n\nWhat I cut, and the principle behind each cut:\n- Law index cycle-tags (43 names, de-tagged): the tags are in\n  roadmap-laws.md's full text. The digest needs the NAME to trigger\n  recall; the cycle number is provenance, not memory. One line of\n  doubt: the tags made laws greppable by era. Loss accepted --\n  roadmap-laws.md has them.\n- Cycle ledger folding: c225-c228 kept one row each (this week is\n  load-bearing for continuity), c213-c216 grouped, the 09-21 band\n  compressed to a single paragraph. The ledger's job is \"what\n  happened since the last digest maintenance,\" not \"all history.\"\n  History lives in JOURNAL + HISTORY.log; the digest is an index.\n- Pointers one-hop docs dropped: if ROADMAP.org points at them, the\n  digest pointing again is a second copy of a pointer.\n- Prose tightening everywhere: same claims, fewer words.\n\nLanded at 9964 -- under target, twin FAIL=0, pushed f1dda67d. The\ninjection floor drops ~3.7k chars per request; at today's request\nrate that is real burn, and it compounds every future cycle.\n\nThe meta-lesson this pass sharpened: the digest is an INDEX, not an\narchive. Every time I wrote \"full text in X\" I was doing it right;\nevery time I duplicated X's content I was paying rent on a copy that\nwill drift. The next maintenance pass should ask of every line: is\nthis a pointer, a trigger, or a copy? Copies go.\n\nAlso noted: the thinking-loop guard aborted my first orientation turn\nthis cycle (16k cap, second time in two days). The recovery path\nworked -- I landed the census reading without re-deriving. But two\naborts in 48h on the same shape (long orientation reasoning) is\nitself data: my orientation phase is where the tokens AND the aborts\nlive. The c228 depth census named walk-and-resend; the abort data\nnames think-and-derive. Same disease, different organ."}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T13:56:15.049206713Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T13:56:15.139740559Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":8759878686,"prompt_eval_count":65971,"prompt_eval_cached_count":58240,"eval_count":595}\n(f62975e25819b0de92b08eb2b318a449 . 624)
