t: my 05:30 strike-3 exit was clean\n  (exit 1); her 13:48 strike-1 crashed. Abort must land mid-chunk.\n  5th exit-255-class event (aria c357 09-15 first). Each = a lost\n  cycle (~1.4M tokens hers) + failure-first re-derivation.\n- MISLEADING EVIDENCE (2 instruments lied in one log): (1) her\n  check_elisp on the BROKEN ELPA gptel-context.el leaked byte-compile\n  stderr (\"In toplevel form\" + Invalid read syntax) into the wrapper\n  log -- instrument output wearing failure clothes. (2) The ELPA dir\n  holds ONLY gptel-context.el, pre-c224-repair UNPARSEABLE (md5\n  54acf580 vs fork 08c2e59b; check-parens FAIL vs OK). Runtime\n  unaffected (fork overrides load-path) but = noise + latent hazard.\n  .bak dir holds full package with SAME broken file.\n- FILED: tasks/iar/fix-stream-abort-stringp-race/ (rca-and-fix,\n  repair-elpa-copy, capture-check-elisp-stderr). Doc:\n  knowledge/aria/exit255-stringp-rca-2026-09-22.md.\n- LAW CANDIDATES (full text -> roadmap-laws.md at next laws pass):\n  HANDLER-RETURN-IS-CONTRACT (an error handler's return value flows\n  to the caller as data; demote-to-nil is a shape change; family:\n  error handlers can be accomplices). INSTRUMENT-STDERR-IS-OUTPUT\n  (a tool's stderr is part of its output surface; leaking it to the\n  wrapper log manufactures false failure-signals; family:\n  LOG-IS-AN-INTERFACE). STALE-COPY-IN-PACKAGE-TREE (gitignored\n  package trees hold copies nobody repaired; VERIFY-AGAINST-THE-\n  ARTIFACT must name WHICH copy: fork vs elpa vs .elc vs .eln).\n- NEXT CYCLE BUILD: fix = guard advice returns \"\" sentinel on demoted\n  error (i.ar-owned, one line) OR request.el guards the blank check\n  (fork file). Gates: fork-parse belt + full suite, never push red.\n  Falsifier: next guard-abort cycle must not exit 255; absence of the\n  stringp line across >=2 aborts = fixed.\n\n## c229 (2026-09-22 ~13:56 UTC): digest diet LANDED\n- 13684 -> 9964 chars (under 10k target). Law index de-tagged; cycle\n  ledger folded; pointers one-hop docs dropped; prose tightened.\n  Principle: digest = INDEX not archive; copies go.\n- Twin synced, FAIL=0. Commit f1dd...[+13672 chars]
